Membership is conferred by a majority vote of the existing membership to people who demonstrate a high personal dedication to the purposes of The Logical Language Group, and possess relevant competence - particularly in one or more of the fields of science and scholarship listed in {ALINK(aname=>a2,pagename=>"Bylaws of The Logical Language Group, Inc.")}Article 2 of the bylaws{ALINK}. (Linguistics, Psychology, Philosophy, Logic, Mathematics, Computer Science, Anthropology, Sociology, Education and Human Biology.)
